From 1194f83ada6b5e0feb1b4a281973c4cb687b8391 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:48:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The owner's latest saved label names a person in the server's
 own lines
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tester's 62340 (55012, 55015): after 0381, search showed the owner's
latest label, but the sent-to sentence and the status list still said
„Helper C" for the person the owner had renamed „Levani". Those lines read
the name through nameAsSavedBySql, which kept the longest clean label, and
the old seat label was the longer one.

The label the owner saved last now wins there, and in the five other
places that show the owner (or a bridge) one saved label: the bridge's own
name for a number, the search via-name, the mediator's label, the daily
contact question and the new-member note. The name matcher in createAsk
keeps the longest match, which is about matching text, not showing it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
